{
  "_documentation": {
    "purpose": "Generic English Remeha heating overview with a linked Details subview.",
    "bindings": "Symbolic entity roles only. Real entity IDs, room names, addresses and local automations belong in a private bindings file or private template.",
    "power": "W; negative readings are displayed as zero, missing or older-than-180-second readings are unavailable.",
    "energy": "Calendar statistics show changes in import energy counters in kWh; live power remains in W.",
    "side_effects": "Generation is offline; controls write only when used. No history, automations or other views are changed.",
    "customization": "Use --template for a private main/detail composition and --insert-after for an optional existing view anchor.",
    "layout": "The system diagram includes compact thermometers, followed by heating, temporary temperature, hot water and electricity. Controls stack on mobile.",
    "schematic": "Requires the bundled remeha-heating-schematic-card.js as a Lovelace module. It reads current HA states and animates recognized modes reported by Remeha. The animation represents the active mode, not a measured flow rate.",
    "temporary": "The override card uses the Home Assistant theme. Presets edit local minutes. Confirmed actions call the shared Remeha and climate services.",
    "unknown": "Unknown, pending and stale states are never treated as confirmed success or as zero.",
    "details": "All 12 duration presets and complete diagnostics remain in the linked Details subview.",
    "automation_controls": "Private extension templates must contain only current local automation controls and instructions. Retire obsolete rows in both linked views. The public template contains no instance-specific automations."
  },
